+## List price is on products
+
+`products.retail_price` is the list price. It is a column of the parquet file,
+so it is queryable even though the model text never declares it. How far below
+list a line sold is `1 - sale_price / products.retail_price`.
+
+## A product field summed over lines
+
+From `order_items`, `products.retail_price.sum()` counts each product once
+(17,525.92: the catalog), while `sum(products.retail_price)` counts it once per
+line (2,218,715.93: list value of everything sold). For anything "per item
+sold", use `sum(products.x)` or `avg(products.x)`; the dotted form is the
+per-product figure.
+
